📌 Resource Management Tool (Power Apps)
Overview
The Resource Management Tool is an enterprise Power Platform application designed to centralize and streamline system access administration, equipment provisioning, and asset tracking for a department of 300+ employees.
Originally modernized from a legacy Microsoft Access database, the solution was expanded with new capabilities to support leadership visibility, asset management, and governance documentation.
The tool ensures:
- New hires receive required equipment and system access on day one
- Existing employees receive appropriate access when cross‑training
- Loaner laptops are tracked, reserved, and returned on time
- Returned assets are documented and traceable
- All system access governance and process documentation is stored in one place

Business Problem
Before this application existed, critical workflows were fragmented across multiple tools:
- System access and workstation requests lived in a legacy Access database
- Loaner laptop availability, TWA/LDA tracking, and return‑to‑stock workflows had no formal process
- Returned assets could only be traced by searching old ServiceNow emails
- RBAC roles, ad hoc access procedures, Power Platform governance, EUC governance, QlikSense governance, and system access process flows were scattered across Word/Excel files in SharePoint
- Leadership had no centralized visibility into requests, assets, or access governance
This created inefficiencies, inconsistent processes, and operational risk.

Solution
The Resource Management Tool consolidates all system access and equipment workflows into a single governed Power App. It provides:
- A unified interface for requesting system access, equipment, and loaner laptops
- Automated routing and notifications for all request types
- Real‑time visibility into request status for both requesters and system admins
- A centralized repository for all RBAC, ad hoc access, and governance documentation
- Asset tracking for loaner laptops and returned equipment
- Integration with other automated processes that track TWA/LDA assignments
The tool serves as the operational hub for system access administration and equipment management across the department.

